# Generated from: specs/386-detect-recoverable-files-labels-during-publication-upgrade/requirements.md
Feature: Canonicalize safely recoverable Files labels during publication upgrade
  Upgrade may repair an exact singular label near miss without weakening delivery authority.

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Singular Files near miss is detected
    Given an admitted task with one valid Files declaration and no canonical declaration
    When publication upgrade detection runs without unrelated dependency collection
    Then it emits a digest-bound rewrite to the exact File(s) label
    And the validated declaration value is preserved

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: PathCast-shaped package rewrites four labels only
    Given admitted tasks T001 through T004 each have one recoverable Files declaration
    When the detected publication action is approved and applied
    Then exactly four labels become canonical
    And all declared paths and unrelated bytes are unchanged
    And repeat detection emits no publication rewrite

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Unsafe declaration states remain findings
    Given a task has missing duplicate mixed ambiguous malformed hidden or unsupported declarations
    When publication upgrade detection runs
    Then no rewrite establishes publication authority for that task
    And a visible file-like declaration is retained as a located finding

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Delivery parser stays fail closed until apply
    Given the PathCast-shaped package uses Files labels
    When the delivery parser evaluates the pre-state
    Then publication_scope_unproven is returned
    When the approved digest-bound rewrite is applied
    Then the delivery parser accepts the complete intended path set only

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Existing canonical value recovery remains supported
    Given a canonical File(s) declaration has an unambiguous recoverable value
    When publication upgrade detection and apply run
    Then the existing canonical value normalization is unchanged
    And the Unreleased changelog records the issue-owned defect fix
